## Why This Is Asked
Tests expertise in fully dynamic Li Chao trees, offline lifetime decomposition, and practical handling of duplicates in production settings.

## Key Concepts
- **Segment tree over time** for lifetime interval decomposition
- **Per-node Li Chao trees** for minimum query aggregation
- **Path-query traversal** across O(log N) nodes
- Memory-time trade-offs for handling large N and duplicates

## Code Example
```javascript
class LiChao {
  insert(line) { /* insert line into this node's Li Chao tree */ }
  query(x) { /* return minimum y at x across stored lines */ }
}

class DynamicLineSet {
  constructor(N) {
    this.segmentTree = new SegmentTree(N);
  }

  addLine(m, b, id, insertTime) {
    const interval = [insertTime, Infinity];
    this.segmentTree.addInterval(interval, { m, b, id });
  }

  removeLine(id, removeTime) {
    // Update the line's interval end time in the segment tree
    this.segmentTree.closeInterval(id, removeTime);
  }

  queryMin(x, queryTime) {
    return this.segmentTree.queryPath(queryTime)
      .reduce((min, lichao) => Math.min(min, lichao.query(x)), Infinity);
  }
}
```

## Complexity Analysis
| Operation | Time | Space |
|-----------|------|-------|
| addLine | O(log N) | O(log N) per line |
| removeLine | O(log N) | - |
| queryMin | O(log² N) | - |

## Edge Cases
- **Identical slopes**: Stored separately with unique ids; Li Chao tree handles min correctly
- **Immediate removal**: Assigned to leaf node only
- **Large N**: Memory scales with O(N log N) total line-node assignments

## Why This Is Asked
Autocomplete systems in product search need fast prefix queries with duplicates. A Trie with per-node counts shows practical memory/time trade-offs and handles duplicates transparently.

## Key Concepts
- Trie with endCount and subCount
- Duplicate handling via counts
- O(|word|) insertion/erasure/lookup
- O(|prefix|) prefix query
- Space proportional to total characters stored

## Code Example
```javascript
class Node { constructor(){ this.next = new Map(); this.end=0; this.sub=0; } }
class Trie { constructor(){ this.root=new Node(); }
  insertWord(w){ let cur=this.root; cur.sub++; for(const ch of w){ if(!cur.next.has(ch)) cur.next.set(ch,new Node()); cur=cur.next.get(ch); cur.sub++; } cur.end++; }
  eraseWord(w){ let cur=this.root; cur.sub--; for(const ch of w){ cur=cur.next.get(ch); cur.sub--; } cur.end--; }
  containsWord(w){ let cur=this.root; for(const ch of w){ if(!cur.next.has(ch)) return false; cur=cur.next.get(ch); } return cur.end>0; }
  countWithPrefix(pref){ let cur=this.root; for(const ch of pref){ if(!cur.next.has(ch)) return 0; cur=cur.next.get(ch); } return cur.sub; }
}
```

